<!--
  CLAUDE.md §2: no user-visible string is hard-coded in Kotlin. Every string in the product lives
  here, in Farsi, even though the app is single-language (PRD §13.3).

  Text comes from the design files, which PRD §0 makes the final authority on in-page copy.

  Note on the ZWNJ (نیم‌فاصله, U+200C): it is present in strings like «حساب‌های بانکی» and
  «بودجه‌بندی». The DS guide calls a wrong ZWNJ the single most visible typographic error in a Farsi
  product, so these must not be "cleaned up" into plain spaces.
-->
